# AutoCAD process lock

Before any build/test that may load or overwrite AutoCAD plugin assemblies
(`AcKrovy.AutoCAD`, solution x64 Debug/Release, Full compatibility gate, NETLOAD path):

1. Invoke the shared `scripts/acad-host-workflow.ps1` when a HOST build is
   required. It checks only `acad.exe`, requests a normal close, waits briefly,
   and force-stops the remaining intended AutoCAD process before the build.
2. Wait until `acad.exe` is actually gone before building; never retry MSB3026
   copy loops against a live AutoCAD process.
3. For portable-only work, a process check is sufficient and the workflow need
   not launch AutoCAD.

Portable Core-only tests/gates that do not touch AutoCAD output may still run
while AutoCAD is open.

After a successful HOST build/test, invoke the same workflow without `-NoLaunch`
to launch AutoCAD Architecture 2027 with the configured saved HOST DWG. The
existing startup/autoload remains responsible for loading the plugin, running
`AK_RUNTIME_BUILD`, and enabling `AK_ROOF_3D_TRACE`; do not add a competing loader.
